advocacy. That page cites Texas leading the nation in nuclear verdicts from 2009 to 2023 (\n207 verdicts over $10 million, totaling more than $45 billion\n) and estimates tort costs at \nabout $4,594 per household\n. The tort-cost figures come from the U.S. Chamber of Commerce's Institute for Legal Reform, and Texans for Lawsuit Reform (TLR) repeats them. Both groups are parties to the tort-reform fight. There is some independent support for part of the claim. A Chamber of Commerce legal-reform study found Texas among the top four nuclear-verdict states, and an NAIC journal article says \nthese verdicts can directly affect the cost and availability of insurance\n.\n\nOfficial and neutral sources do not give litigation as the main cause of Texas's rising insurance costs. Texas Insurance Commissioner Amanda Crawford told lawmakers on Oct. 5 that \nsevere weather, high inflationary costs impacting home repairs and \"the concentration of risk\"\n caused the rise in home insuranc", "verdict_sources": ["https://www.insurancecouncil.org/lawsuit-abuse/", "https://www.tortreform.com/newsletters/tlr-weekly-news-roundup-december-10-2025/", "https://communityimpact.com/central-austin/texas-legislature/experts-hardening-homes-against-disasters-could-drive-down-texas-home-insurance-costs/", "https://www.dallasfed.org/research/swe/2026/swe2609", "https://www.texasmonthly.com/news-politics/home-insurance-skyrocketing-texas-legislature/", "https://content.naic.org/sites/default/files/cipr-jir-2023-3.pdf"], "posts": 1, "views": 177763, "accounts": 1, "copies": 0, "pushback_posts": 0, "lanes": [{"key": "lawsuit_abuse_hidden_tax", "label": "Lawsuit abuse as hidden tax", "color": "#3987e5", "posts": 1}], "first_seen": "2026-10-07T20:46:50+00:00", "first_handle": "pactconsumers", "first_handles": ["pactconsumers"], "first_url": "https://x.com/pactconsumers/status/2107935706433663260", "first_source": "x", "first_name": "Protecting American Consumers Together (PACT)", "sources": {"x": {"p